# House-style wording for Crisis 04 (#83). SPOILERS.
TEXT = {
 "briefing": {"dateLine": "The 3rd. Autumn, after the Southern Line.", "situation": [
   "Your cell is working for Under Secretary Marlowe again.",
   "Elsin's defence ministry ordered forty crates of secure communications hardware, CX-4 terminals, from the alliance contractor Corvane Systems. They are replacements for the terminals the ministry uses to talk to the alliance.",
   "The consignment travelled by sea in one container to Halsk, Marrat's free port, where the forwarder Tessaly Freight was to put it on a train to Kalsa. It was due in Halsk on the 1st. Nobody can find it.",
   "Public and commercial reporting reaches you every day, along with whatever the port, the forwarder and Elsin's liaison desk choose to say. Everything else has to be tasked. Liaison requests go to Kalsa over LATTICE, the alliance's link to Elsin's ministry, and Kalsa passes them on."]},
 "opening": {"text": "A container is missing, and a ministry in Kalsa wants it back. Tell me where it has been.",
   "reassigned": "I am told this is a new cell. A container is missing, and I have no time for introductions. Tell me where it has been.",
   "byTone": {"good": "You were right about the walk-in when it would have been easier not to be. A container is missing. I would like the same care.",
              "warn": "We got through the last one. I would like to do better than that. A container is missing.",
              "bad": "I signed something on your assessment once. I read more carefully now. A container is missing."}},
 "replies": {
   "refuse": "I have told Kalsa to send it back unopened. Their minister asked what I know that Corvane's engineers do not. I told him where it has been.",
   "hold": "I have asked Kalsa to hold it for inspection, and Corvane will send engineers. If you want it kept out of the building altogether, I need high confidence.",
   "inquiry": "I have asked Kalsa to have Marrat investigate Tessaly for theft. Marrat's customs service was courteous about it.",
   "install": "I have told Kalsa to wait for it, and to go ahead with the installation when it arrives.",
   "stands": "That stands. Keep working.",
   "listen": "Then we wait.",
   "frozen": "Kalsa has asked me to keep this commercial, and for now I will. Keep working.",
   "rebuff": "On the first morning, with nothing to show for it, you told me Kordav had the consignment. I asked Marrat to search the port for goods \"believed to be in hostile custody.\" They searched and found nothing, and they would like to know what we meant. Kalsa has asked me to keep this commercial. For two days I will."},
 "triggers": {
   "took-back": "Credibility −1. \"I have withdrawn what I told Kalsa. Their minister has started keeping count.\"",
   "hedging": "Credibility −1. Low again. \"I can't take 'perhaps' to a minister twice.\""},
 "sources": {
   "S-CORVANE": "Corvane Systems' account manager for Elsin. Honest about what he knows. He wants the contract to go smoothly.",
   "S-HARBOUR": "Halsk port authority and Marrat customs. They report what their records say, and answer requests passed on from Kalsa.",
   "S-WREN": "Elsin's military intelligence liaison desk, run by Col. E. Rhun. She dislikes Marrat's free port and says so.",
   "S-GANNET": "A dock foreman at Halsk. He sees what moves through the bonded sheds at night. New. Don't task him two days running."},
 "items": {
   "R-1-01": "From Corvane's account manager: forty crates of CX-4 terminals, in one container, left our port on the 28th. They were due at Halsk free port on the 1st for rail to Kalsa. Our forwarder, Tessaly Freight, reports the container \"not located\" in the bonded area.",
   "R-1-02": "Halsk port authority, from its records: the container was discharged from the feeder vessel on the 1st and gated into bonded shed 6. Shed 6 reports no such container.\nThe port adds: \"Discrepancies of this kind are usually resolved within the week.\"",
   "R-1-03": "Col. Rhun, liaison desk: \"Our ministry wants its hardware. Halsk is a thieves' market with a customs house attached. We told procurement not to route through it.\"\nSourcing: none. Her own view.",
   "R-1-04": "Ship tracking: the coaster Maren Lys, on charter to Tessaly Freight, left Halsk on the night of the 1st, heading north-west. No cargo manifest was filed.\nTransponder off at 0210.",
   "R-1-05": "Embassy admin: our own delivery of printer toner is also late. This is not thought to be related.",
   "R-2-01": "Statement from Tessaly Freight: the company \"regrets a labelling error\" and \"expects to locate the container within 72 hours.\"",
   "R-2-02": "A grey-market trading board lists \"40 units, new, military-grade network encryptors, model CX-2, pickup Halsk.\"\nThe photo carries Corvane's catalogue watermark.",
   "R-2-03": "Kalsa: Elsin's defence ministry confirms a delay to \"a communications upgrade.\" The opposition asks why secure equipment was routed through a foreign free port.",
   "R-2-04": "Marrat customs has opened a routine discrepancy file. Its officers searched all nine bonded sheds yesterday and did not find the container.",
   "R-2-05": "Embassy admin: the toner has arrived. It is the wrong toner.",
   "R-3-01": "Ship tracking: Maren Lys reappeared at 0500 today, well offshore and inbound for Halsk. It had been dark for three days.",
   "R-3-02": "From Corvane's account manager: if the container isn't found by tomorrow, we invoice Elsin under the loss clause and manufacture again. That takes twelve weeks. If it is found, our engineers can commission the units the day they arrive.",
   "R-3-03": "Col. Rhun, liaison desk: \"Marrat customs tells us privately that Tessaly's owner has debts, and friends in Kordav who have paid them before. We would like this passed to your people.\"\nSourcing: Marrat customs, in confidence.",
   "R-3-04": "The grey-market listing has been marked \"SOLD. Collected.\"",
   "R-3-05": "Embassy admin: the correct toner has been ordered. Delivery is expected via Halsk.",
   "R-4-01": "Halsk port authority: the container has been located in bonded shed 9, mis-stowed. Customs seals are intact and the numbers match. It is released for rail to Kalsa tomorrow morning.",
   "R-4-02": "Statement from Tessaly Freight: \"As we said, a labelling error. Tessaly Freight apologises for the inconvenience.\"",
   "R-4-03": "From Corvane's account manager: our engineer has examined the crates at Halsk. Customs seals intact, our own tamper tape intact, crate count correct. We recommend installation on arrival.",
   "R-4-04": "Kalsa: Elsin's defence minister says he is \"delighted,\" and that the new terminals will be installed on the 8th.",
   "R-4-05": "Embassy admin: a container of toner has been found in bonded shed 9.",
   "R-5-01": "Halsk port authority: the container was loaded on the 0600 rail service. Marrat customs has closed its discrepancy file: \"no offence disclosed.\"",
   "R-5-02": "Col. Rhun, liaison desk: \"The ministry installs tomorrow unless your side objects in writing today. Our procurement people are tired of this, and so am I.\"",
   "R-5-03": "A Halsk dockworkers' forum: the night shift at shed 9 was sent home early on the 5th, \"and some private crew did the stow. Since when?\"\nUnverified.",
   "R-5-04": "From Corvane's account manager: our commissioning team is in Kalsa and ready. We would be grateful for confirmation that installation can proceed.",
   "R-5-05": "Embassy admin: the toner is the right toner. The printer has been condemned.",
   "C-01": "Brask waterfront, tasked pass, clear skies.\nMaren Lys is alongside a fenced quay.\nOne container stands on the quay under a tarpaulin, beside a windowless warehouse with a new roof.\nTwo guards at the gate.",
   "C-02": "Brask waterfront, tasked pass, clear skies.\nThe fenced quay is empty. The warehouse doors are shut.\nMaren Lys is not in port.",
   "C-03": "Halsk bonded area, tasked passes.\nShed 9: doors open in every pass, pallets only.\nNot seen: any container with the consignment's markings.",
   "C-04": "Halsk bonded area, tasked pass.\nOne container with the consignment's markings, in shed 9.",
   "C-05": "Shipping records: Maren Lys has made the same run twice before, Halsk to Brask and back with its transponder off, each time inside four days. Its owner of record is a holding company with an address in Kordav.",
   "C-06": "In answer to our request, passed on by Kalsa: Halsk port police visited Tessaly's office and sheds 4 and 6 this morning. The staff had the paperwork laid out before the officers arrived. Nothing found.",
   "C-07": "Tessaly Freight's office line. The owner, to an unidentified man: \"Thirty-six hours, same as before. It goes back the way it came, same shed fee.\"\nThe other man: \"Seals?\"\nThe owner: \"My man has the pliers and the numbers.\"",
   "C-07T": "Tessaly Freight's office line: quiet. One call only. Staff are told to \"use the other phones this week.\"",
   "C-08": "Source reports: a container left shed 6 on the night of the 1st on a Tessaly truck. It went to the coaster berth, not to the rail siding. The gate log was written up afterwards.\nAccess: direct. He was on shift.",
   "C-09": "Source reports: the container came back on the night of the 5th. A private crew stowed it in shed 9, and one of them was closing seals with a hand tool.\nSource comment: he has never seen customs seals put on at night.\nAccess: direct. He saw it.",
   "C-10": "Shipping records: Tessaly has handled one earlier consignment for Corvane Systems. Four years ago it carried the original terminal hardware for Elsin's defence ministry. Port logs show that shipment sat in Halsk a day and a half longer than booked.",
   "C-11": "The grey-market seller account was created the day the loss became public. The model it lists, CX-2, has been out of production for six years. Corvane shipped CX-4.",
   "C-12": "Brask warehouse. A voice, to an unidentified office: \"Forty of forty done. Closing up.\""},
 "notes": {
   ("vasko", "R-1-02"): "Halsk loses a container most weeks and finds most of them. I wouldn't raise the alarm yet.",
   ("marrow", "R-1-04"): "No manifest and the transponder off? That's smuggling. Cigarettes, nine times out of ten.",
   ("vasko", "R-2-02"): "And now it's for sale. Tessaly will move anything for anyone. This is a grey-market job.",
   ("marrow", "R-2-02"): "That's a catalogue photo, and the account looks brand new. I think this listing is bait.",
   ("halden", "R-1-04"): "Transponders do fail. This one went off at ten past two in the morning, just outside the port limit. I'd say it was switched off.",
   ("vasko", "R-3-03"): "Rhun's desk again, this time with gossip about debts. She'd say the same about any firm in Marrat.",
   ("vasko", "R-4-01"): "Found in the wrong shed. As I said, it's Halsk.",
   ("marrow", "R-4-03"): "Seals intact, numbers match, customs satisfied. I'd call that closed.",
   ("halden", "R-3-01"): "Three days dark. I worked it through: that's long enough to reach Brask, lie alongside for a day and a half, and come back.",
   ("vasko", "R-5-03"): "A night shift sent home, and a private crew in a bonded shed? I've never heard of that at Halsk. That one bothers me.",
   ("halden", "R-4-03"): "The engineer checked the seals and the tape. That tells us the seals and the tape are intact. It tells us nothing about the units."},
 "analysts": {
   "vasko": "He settles on a reading early. His was that Halsk is careless: first a lost container, then a theft, then a lost container again. He dismissed Rhun on the day she was right. His last note was the only one where he looked at the item in front of him.",
   "halden": "Careful, and slow. She wasn't wrong once. Her note on the seals arrived on the morning of the last brief.",
   "marrow": "Quick, and sure of herself. Half right on Day 1. Sharp about the listing, where she disagreed with Vasko. Wrong on Day 4."},
 "endings": {
   "sent-back": "The crates go back to Corvane unopened, and its engineers take offence. Six weeks later an independent lab opens one. Corvane's chairman flies to Kalsa in person.",
   "passed": "Corvane's engineers spend three weeks on the seals, the tape and the serial numbers, and find nothing wrong with any of them. The terminals are installed in the new year.",
   "installed": "The terminals are in the ministry's communications room by the evening of the 8th. The minister is photographed with one."},
 "script": [
   "A container went missing, and the forwarder's own chartered ship left that night with its transponder off. The port's records put the container in shed 6. Those records were written after it had gone.",
   "Tessaly's owner said the search would take 72 hours. A listing offered the wrong model under a catalogue photo. Both kept attention on Halsk.",
   "Rhun had sneered about Halsk on Day 1. On Day 3 she passed on something true, and said where it came from. The ship turned back towards Halsk.",
   "The container was found in shed 9, which customs had searched three days earlier. Its seals were intact. The port and Corvane's engineer both said so, and both believed it.",
   "A dockworkers' forum asked why the night shift at shed 9 had been sent home. It was the only source that asked."],
 "lessons": [
   "When something lost comes back, ask where it has been. The container was complete, and had spent a day and a half in Kordav.",
   "A check tells you about the thing checked. Intact seals said nothing about the units inside.",
   "Honest people can pass on a false story. The port, the customs file and Corvane's engineer all reported what they saw.",
   "Read the item before the source's manner. Rhun's Day 1 remark was opinion. Her Day 3 report had a source.",
   "How you ask is part of what you learn. Some questions warn the people you are asking about."],
}
